  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Read gh issue view 2015 in full and DI-104 in notes/defer-issues.md. The Decision Records tab is built Signal-first: GET /api/v1/signals/worklist?set=decided lists decided Signals and attaches the record sprk_signal.sprk_decisionrecord points to (Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs DecidedFetch, ReadDecisionRecordsAsync). A Signal reviewed twice (Send inquiry, then the decision) shows only the later record, and email-gate Decision Records (D-139, no Signal) never appear. Owner decision D-231: read Decision Records first; gate records are listed with their summary and no Open action. Keep the writer-authorship rule (WriterCreatedRecord, task 223) and the caller-read rules: core-record grouping via the existing stamps (D-34/D-36), secure children only to the family (D-33/D-123), no-core records owner-only (D-35/D-39). Client: the tab in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (find it from the decided-set consumer). Line numbers at origin/master d43fc9e16d; search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: .NET 10 BFF read routes as the caller, FetchXML, React/Fluent v9 shared components.</role>
  <goal>The Decision Records tab lists every writer-authored Decision Record the caller can read in the window, including each review of a Signal reviewed more than once and email-gate records (shown without Open), and nothing the caller cannot read or that the writer did not create.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Prefer extending the decided-set read over a new route (root §11). The window stays as today (check the code; the issue says 90 days on sprk_decidedon). Existing Open behaviour for Signal-backed records is unchanged (reopens read-only). Keep the response contract additive and update the contract baseline in the same PR. Check the worklist row layout rules in project CLAUDE.md §2 UI and D-227 for wording.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
